#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152149 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bb0eba0-05b2-5908-9abc-74cddff4d1e1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e05b1e5-a40e-54fd-9b04-d5dca64f71b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254083} {:answer/id #uuid "4dfd14db-f28a-5907-bae0-c07e9ca18570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254341} {:answer/id #uuid "5616af10-5723-542b-9fd4-3b9b76730524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254427} {:answer/id #uuid "922d36ec-1c65-5bf2-9934-84d3bfa56c5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254951} {:answer/id #uuid "f392c96c-38da-5421-a0e9-e7d801f6a160" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e05b1e5-a40e-54fd-9b04-d5dca64f71b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254083} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbc83de8-3399-50c2-a721-1d19605f5c25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256256}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "acabb8ff-4a50-5eab-8825-59e98be4e24d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122963" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [0,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=10-2x-y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={1,3},\\,{P}_{2}={0,1,2,3},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/40/40eb21cbafdbd721ac8f1710d52918d5e463fa3ffc6eb06aeba8539eb53c7db8.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{13}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{13})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=2$ for all $3$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=2{m}_{11}+2{m}_{12}+2{m}_{13}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=10-2x-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=10-2x-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/c1/c17b413125919726cd1aba9efdc4dcb5949fee52947610abcbb952f1b7917281.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/5d/5dbf341642f5e15942323ec3d5674fc361f0b48d9cabd5f54c7fedb95a3f6fb6.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(3,1)=3 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(3,2)=2 \\\\ {m}_{31} & =f(3,3)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 1=12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256764 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152148 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "30328c9f-afbd-5fd7-b32a-90717a813001" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f7999b8-b233-5c53-8825-7de78eea7f1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253808} {:answer/id #uuid "260fa322-ead1-5a86-9218-41aaf1516f5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254008} {:answer/id #uuid "9d99e890-0a44-5df1-af7d-00eeaad8fc09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255055} {:answer/id #uuid "a13c9ea8-e7c6-5b02-81b7-87b7c9a73a22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255088} {:answer/id #uuid "cc63917c-9227-514c-861c-c65220955f1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc63917c-9227-514c-861c-c65220955f1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255487} :answer-field/id #uuid "17b5d493-1477-5182-82d2-93e08771b9bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b5b65c6c-6196-523c-833d-8bae70c92a8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-122983" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [0,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+y+1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={0,2},\\,{P}_{2}={0,1,2,3},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/73/7310b1302c35084aaef5a8b2316f59c0fbd806bc9314a51fe77167988d01f343.png)\n\nThe lower sum $L(f,P)$ is given by \n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{13}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{13})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=2$ for all $3$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=2{m}_{11}+2{m}_{12}+2{m}_{13}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+y+1$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+y+1$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ce/ce58eb1c2ee59cf97aa77fb9e840578e7a99f094b11b2e282317aad69ae31b7a.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/ce/cec70986dea862392342377d83adbfa534ce0f3aa87cf2161c2f88eb83fbed58.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(0,0)=1 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(0,1)=2 \\\\ {m}_{13} & =f(0,2)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & =2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152148 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "30328c9f-afbd-5fd7-b32a-90717a813001" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51e27ca0-b1f0-501d-8d8a-15d892923c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342916} {:answer/id #uuid "69fa31fd-299d-521f-935b-b7bc44d987ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343143} {:answer/id #uuid "9011bf66-d25a-5f40-81fc-8d7cc4f3a6e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343495} {:answer/id #uuid "e1dece52-db3a-5167-887d-cab95aa2752c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344226} {:answer/id #uuid "fd7ce6f3-9dae-58d1-a27e-ed19aa7aaaab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51e27ca0-b1f0-501d-8d8a-15d892923c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342916} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee7e2232-ee64-5a5c-ba90-c8733c5e655d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "591dbb3d-401d-5ba1-98ad-e1bc0718cda4" :question/math-academy-id "q-75248" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+y-1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={1,2,3},\\,{P}_{2}={0,1,2},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/3b/3be0ba3fa44ba61e0b55500e588387cd087b8d2f2687c5636c9b053f1f8dc5d6.png)\n\nThe lower sum $L(f,P)$ is given by \n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y-1$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y-1$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/b3/b3c2a3891860a8ad88d2f111a3e279a65398a37020ab2f0843f8475dfd38df15.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/76/76cbbcf7ddff625cf035d6f7e37acbc6d278734cc87648ef6a88f8ace61f731e.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,0)=0 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,0)=1 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(1,1)=1 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,1)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & =0+1+1+2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345058 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152149 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bb0eba0-05b2-5908-9abc-74cddff4d1e1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57a03b7d-8141-5d28-a86e-2499e1398aea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342970} {:answer/id #uuid "6e80cc3e-2714-55da-bfca-0054503bf050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343188} {:answer/id #uuid "7ba6b947-6e76-544f-ad92-7e25df4c2244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343300} {:answer/id #uuid "f3915db4-6e1c-5806-94b9-0e54df842dd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344380} {:answer/id #uuid "ff44fa67-8e68-5cb5-bb53-95c06c461de1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3915db4-6e1c-5806-94b9-0e54df842dd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344380} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2394566-b7eb-566f-8fd0-125f8b6baf2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a7c41781-bde2-5bb7-ab42-7938c0b39776" :question/math-academy-id "q-75255" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=13-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={0,1,2},\\,{P}_{2}={1,2,3},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/4f/4faf932e63a57d2fe53fb3942cfe21c65d0d2a88692c665b2706bd68164855c9.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=13-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=13-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/e7/e70e2cf07b27a91c34e59435229302f3b2127b15a2f39049c0a8389cd6f59863.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/aa/aa3858dba149ebf5650ed06f75444244494fe0a961f897100914d54f6d7c0b49.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,2)=8 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,2)=5 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(1,3)=3 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,3)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=8+5+3+0=16.\n$$"}]}
